claim.claim-text:
a chamber (106) defined by a chamber housing (102) extending between a first end region (102a) and a second end region (102b) and including an opening (103) for providing a liquid to the chamber;
a lid (104) attached to the opening that moves between a closed position and an open position;
a tooth (124) that snap fits to a complementary surface on the chamber housing to move the lid from the open position to the closed position in response to a rapid motion of the apparatus;
a liquid dispensing outlet (130) through which the liquid is dispensed during use;
a handle portion (114) located below the chamber, the handle portion mounted to the chamber housing and proximal to the first end region; and
a body configured to present the opening when the lid is in the open position so that water flows into the chamber via the opening at an accelerated rate when the apparatus is moving.
